  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_residual_block(x: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Residual Block** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_residual_block(x: list) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(x, dtype=np.float32)\n    out = arr + np.maximum(0.0, arr * 0.5)\n    return np.round(np.maximum(0.0, out), 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
